---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Santiago González',
  url: 'https://brandsbuilders.ca/about',
  jobTitle: 'Founder',
  worksFor: { '@id': 'https://brandsbuilders.ca/#business' },
  sameAs: ['https://brandsbuilders.ca'],
};

const seo = {
  title: 'About — BrandsBuilders | Santiago González',
  description: 'BrandsBuilders builds websites and runs ad campaigns for cleaning companies in Calgary and the surrounding area, backed by a 30-day guarantee.',
  canonical: 'https://brandsbuilders.ca/about',
  schema: personSchema,
};
---

<Layout seo={seo}>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-white pt-16 pb-14 border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 text-orange-700 text-xs font-semibold mb-6">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-orange-500 shrink-0"></span>
        BrandsBuilders
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-5 leading-tight">
        Built by Santiago González
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        I build websites and run the ad campaigns for cleaning companies in Calgary and the surrounding area — so owners can spend their time cleaning, not chasing leads or fighting with a template site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Story -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none space-y-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-[17px]">

        <p>
          A lot of cleaning businesses I came across in Calgary were running on word of mouth and a Facebook page — good at the work itself, but with no real website and no ads bringing in new clients. Meanwhile a competitor with a decent site and a couple of ad campaigns running was picking up the residential and commercial jobs they were missing out on.
        </p>

        <p>
          The gap wasn't the quality of the cleaning. It was that nobody searching "cleaning company Calgary" could find them, and nobody was running ads to put them in front of the right homeowners or businesses.
        </p>

        <p>
          So I built one offer specifically for that: a real website, plus the Google and Meta ad campaigns run on your behalf — pointed at residential clients, commercial contracts, or both, depending on which side of the business you want to grow.
        </p>

        <p>
          I back it with a 30-day guarantee. If you're not happy with the website or how the ads are being managed in that first month, I refund what you paid me for the work. Ad spend paid directly to Google or Meta is separate — it never comes to me, so it isn't part of the refund. I'd rather say that upfront than have it be a surprise later.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values / How I work -->
  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-16 border-y border-gray-200">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">How I work</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        {[
          { title: 'Honest about fit', body: 'If your business isn\'t ready for ad spend yet, I\'ll tell you that on the call — not after you\'ve paid.' },
          { title: 'You own the website', body: 'The site is yours. No lock-in on the build itself, no data held hostage.' },
          { title: 'One point of contact', body: 'You deal with me directly — not an account manager or an outsourced team.' },
          { title: 'Backed by a guarantee', body: 'Not happy in the first 30 days? I refund what you paid for the work — no arguments.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-gray-900 text-white py-16 text-center">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Run a cleaning company in Calgary?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8 text-lg">Book a 15-min call. I'll tell you honestly what the website + ad management would look like for your business before you decide anything.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/apply" class="inline-flex px-9 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 bg-white hover:bg-gray-100 transition text-lg">
          Get my free growth plan →
        </a>
        <a href="https://cal.com/brandsbuilders/30-min" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex px-9 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold text-white border border-gray-700 hover:border-gray-500 transition text-lg">
          Book a 15-min call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
